This project has NO third-party dependencies.

  Standing:  The maze geometry on BOTH engines comes from a shared
             deterministic kernel that is MADFAM's own authoring:
             `maze_kernel.scad` on the OpenSCAD side and its verbatim Python
             twin inlined in maze_coaster.py, maze_cube.py and
             maze_cylinder.py. It is a 32-bit linear congruential generator
             (Numerical Recipes constants — a published parameter triple, not
             copyrightable expression) driving an iterative recursive
             backtracker. Both halves walk cells and neighbours in the same
             fixed order and draw the PRNG at the same points, so the two
             engines carve the same maze for the same `seed`.

  History:   Revisions of the .scad sources before 2026-09-05 called dotSCAD's
             `mz_square`, `mz_squarewalls` and `line2d`
             (https://github.com/JustinSDK/dotSCAD, Justin Lin (@JustinSDK),
             LGPL-3.0), resolved at render time from OPENSCADPATH and never
             vendored here. Those calls have been REMOVED: dotSCAD's maze
             generator draws from its own RNG, which the CadQuery side has no
             way to reproduce, so the two engines rendered different mazes
             from identical parameters. The shared kernel above replaces it.
             No dotSCAD source code was, or is, distributed in this
             repository, and none of it was copied into the kernel.
             Ruled acceptable 2026-09-05 (operator checklist, item G21); the
             dependency it ruled on no longer exists as of item G27.
